WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.470
-My first guest tonight is
one of the biggest movie stars

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.704
in the world.
-Whoo!

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.140
-Her new movie "Black Widow" --
Yeah, ow!

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.842
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.376
"Black Widow" is in theaters

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.847
and on Disney+
with Premiere Access July 9th.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.482
Here is Scarlett Johansson!

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.985
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.187
-Come on, now!
-Hello.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.622
-Ah!

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.758
It is good to see you.
-Hi!

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:25.791
-Hi, bud.

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:27.393
-How's it going?
-It's going great.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.261
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:30.997
I haven't seen you
since you got married.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.231
Congratulations.

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:36.536
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.605
-I wanted to -- There's
many questions I want to ask,

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:43.342
but a couple questions if you
don't mind about you and Colin.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:44.810
We love Colin Jost.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:51.250
And we know you're both
lifelong New Yorkers.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.553
Do you ever argue
over pizza in New York,

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:56.255
where to get the best pizza?

00:00:56.255 --> 00:01:00.192
-Oh, yeah, well, you know,
Colin is from Staten Island,

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:02.662
so that means something.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.930
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.131
You know, he really -- he's --

00:01:06.131 --> 00:01:08.834
he's very specific
about his slice.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:13.038
He'll definitely tell you the
best slice is in Staten Island.

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:14.908
-No, no, no.
-I respect that.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.509
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.044
I respectfully disagree.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:23.949
I am from Manhattan,
and I -- you know, my --

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:27.454
Are you asking where
my favorite slice is from?

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.355
-Yeah.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:33.292
-I got to say, by the slice,
I really love Joe's Pizza.

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:35.695
-That's what I'm talking about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:38.198
Yeah, me too.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:40.500
-I would say
for a whole pie though,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.734
I got to go with Lombardi's.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.902
I love Lombardi's.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.171
-Oh!

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.340
-Yeah.
-Yeah. It's all so good.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.375
It just makes me miss going out
and getting pizza.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.345
But Arturo's is somewhere
on that list too.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:55.181
-Oh, yeah, Arturo's, yeah.
-Love that jam.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.882
"Black Widow," finally.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.584
"Black Widow" is here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.584 --> 00:01:59.952
It's happening!

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:01.520
Are you excited
that it's finally out?

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.955
I mean, are you freaking out?

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.289
It's finally out.

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:06.859
-I am definitely excited.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:11.264
I'm nervous about it, but it's
like a nervous excitement.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.933
But I have been -- You know,
we've been sitting on this film

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:19.238
for over a year, and it's been
10 years in the making.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.607
I'm super proud of it.
-Yeah.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:24.543
-And people seem to really be
responding well to it,

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:26.712
which is fantastic.
-That's right.

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:30.516
-It really is a great movie
to see in the theater

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:33.752
because it's super cinematic,

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:37.857
explosive, loud,
fun, passionate.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.292
-That's what we want! Let's go!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:42.761
-Yeah, it's really great.

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:44.397
It's explosive.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.366
-Is there any Easter eggs that
you can go like,

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.934
well, okay, maybe you can
give me one like,

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.704
are we finally going to get to
know what happened in Budapest?

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:55.875
-Yes, you finally get to know
what happens in "Budapesht."

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.210
-Mm!
-See what I did there?

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.979
-Yeah, you said "pesht."
That's right.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.982
-I said "pesht."
-Yep, you said "pesht."

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.184
Have you been to Budapesht?

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:07.353
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.789
-I have been to Budapesht.

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:13.326
-Yeah, see, I haven't. That's
why I pronounce it Budapest.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.794
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:18.197
-Oh, yeah, you finally learn how
to say Budapesht in this movie.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:21.033
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:25.571
-Yes, you get to find out
what happened in Budapest.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:30.910
You really -- Yeah, you get
to -- I'm always so bad at this.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.912
Let me see. What can I say?

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:39.018
I can say that, okay, you --
You know what?

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.486
You get to -- Ugh.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:41.720
I can't!

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.556
[ Laughter ]
I can't say anything!

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.158
-You can't say anything!

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.192
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.192 --> 00:03:48.594
Because you can't say anything,

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:52.431
I'm trying to think, well, yeah,
you can't say anything.

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:53.432
No, I can't say is
he going to be in it.

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:55.401
-What can I tell you
about the movie?

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.703
Hmm?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.405
What? What happened?

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:02.942
-Well, just blink
if it's going to happen.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.945
-Okay.
If what's going to happen?

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.013
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.214
-Just blink if
it's going to happen.

00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:10.916
-Are you --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.952
My eyes are still open.
-Yep.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.954
So it's not going to happen.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.656
Alright. Good.
So it's not going to happen.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.657
We confirmed right here
on our show

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:21.760
